#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489249 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124451 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0015e19e-222b-5c5b-a020-93392c50c10e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Best Linear Approximation of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f7d0aa5-2342-5d6f-a521-a62d6d54725c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈-\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{x}{108}+\\frac{y}{54}+\\frac{z}{54}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488506} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8e5783-e729-5001-b425-9bd95d7f94c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{x}{108}-\\frac{y}{54}-\\frac{z}{54}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488619} {:answer/id #uuid "52aebee7-a1be-5094-b50c-2fecab43978c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈-\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{x}{108}-\\frac{y}{108}-\\frac{z}{108}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488628} {:answer/id #uuid "8b357635-83ca-53f3-be6f-efc2212bf65c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{x}{108}+\\frac{y}{54}+\\frac{z}{54}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488749} {:answer/id #uuid "bac0b568-47cf-5aed-a2d1-d6ae3ec5aafb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{x}{54}-\\frac{y}{54}-\\frac{z}{54}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c8e5783-e729-5001-b425-9bd95d7f94c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)≈\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{x}{108}-\\frac{y}{54}-\\frac{z}{54}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488619} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5948ebf-b36f-50ef-996a-235488992a7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9d2fd7c0-6fec-5b30-98fe-3b0bf10ba9a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-65338" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,4,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,4,4)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(2,4,4)+∇f(2,4,4)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-4,z-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(2,4,4)=\\frac{1}{6}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =-\\frac{x}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{x}(2,4,4)=-\\frac{2}{{({2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2})}^{3/2}}=-\\frac{1}{108}, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =-\\frac{y}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{y}(2,4,4)=-\\frac{4}{{({2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2})}^{3/2}}=-\\frac{1}{54}, \\\\ {f}_{z} & =-\\frac{z}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{z}(2,4,4)=-\\frac{4}{{({2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2})}^{3/2}}=-\\frac{1}{54}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(2,4,4)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(2,4,4) & =⟨{f}_{x}(2,4,4),{f}_{y}(2,4,4),{f}_{z}(2,4,4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{108},-\\frac{1}{54},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(2,4,4)+∇f(2,4,4)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-4,z-4⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}+⟨-\\frac{1}{108},-\\frac{1}{54},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-4,z-4⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{108}(x-2)-\\frac{1}{54}(y-4)-\\frac{1}{54}(z-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{x}{108}+\\frac{1}{54}-\\frac{y}{54}+\\frac{4}{54}-\\frac{z}{54}+\\frac{4}{54} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{x}{108}-\\frac{y}{54}-\\frac{z}{54}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125255 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124610 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1639105-dca4-50d1-8d86-a7aed03ba0b5" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Value of a Three-Variable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87af71d8-c14b-5e93-8a58-f967155726ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124131} {:answer/id #uuid "8c132d2f-f0e1-55c6-8681-fe71e2237c65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124132} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3bd8a9-f201-5d6b-bf76-51931b9ad32b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.06" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124133} {:answer/id #uuid "d42ce0c3-890f-5ac1-a33f-8104d2a260ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.91" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124134} {:answer/id #uuid "46c19a80-75d5-5b32-b217-f47c15153172" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87af71d8-c14b-5e93-8a58-f967155726ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124131} :answer-field/id #uuid "b665f142-dd59-559d-9742-e6ed101ab440" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d1a53d9-3ef8-57e5-86e4-66648db12db7" :question/math-academy-id "q-97877" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(2,-2,-1)=4,\\,{f}_{x}(2,-2,-1)=2,\\,{f}_{y}(2,-2,-1)=-2,\\,{f}_{z}(2,-2,-1)=-4.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,-2,-1)$ estimate the value of $f(2.02,-1.98,-1.05)$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,-2,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(2,-2,-1)+∇f(2,-2,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y+2,z+1⟩ \\\\  & =f(2,-2,-1)+⟨{f}_{x}(2,-2,-1),{f}_{y}(2,-2,-1),{f}_{z}(2,-2,-1)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,y+2,z+1⟩ \\\\  & =4+⟨2,-2,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,y+2,z+1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(2.02,-1.98,-1.05)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=2.02,$ $y=-1.98,$ and $z=-1.05$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2.02,-1.98,-1.05) & ≈4+⟨2,-2,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨2.02-2,-1.98+2,-1.05+1⟩ \\\\  & =4+⟨2,-2,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨0.02,0.02,-0.05⟩ \\\\  & =4+(0.04-0.04+0.2) \\\\  & =4.2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
